# EFL (differential chief-ray estimate) and SYSPROP (the first-order report) on the manual's
# Cassegrain (cmdref: Ray Tracing).  Before a propagation SYSPROP prints the aperture/wavelength/EFL
# block and a hint; after INT at the focal plane it adds the pixel-based lines (lambda/D per px,
# plate scale).  Measured 2026-10-16 (PLAN_CONSOLIDATION 1.2): after an OPD alone the pixel lines
# print a pitch of 4.4e-12 -- OPD is not a propagation; use INT or PIX, as this journal does.
old $ROOT/docs/macos-manual/examples/Cassegrain.in
efl
sysprop
5
int 5
/null
sysprop
5
# EXPECT: Estimated system effective focal length =\s+22\.47362822690\d+
# EXPECT: Estimated system focal ratio =\s+5\.6184070567\d+
# EXPECT: Entrance pupil diameter \(m\)\s+=\s+4\.0000000E\+00
# EXPECT: lambda/D \(arcsec\)\s+=\s+5\.1566202E-02
# EXPECT: F-number\s+=\s+5\.6184071E\+00
# EXPECT: Nyquist focal sampling \(BaseUnits\) =\s+2\.8092035E-06
# EXPECT: pixel-based plate scale needs a diffraction
# EXPECT: Peak occurs at i=\s+129, j=\s+129
# EXPECT: lambda/D \(detector px\)\s+=\s+5\.2290937E\+00
# EXPECT: Plate scale \(arcsec/px\)\s+=\s+9\.8614033E-03
# EXPECT-NOT: Need source at infinity
# EXPECT-NOT: forrtl
